      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "We will use the distributive property, which is given by:\n\\[\na(b + c) = ab + ac\n\\]\nApplying this to \\((2x + 3)(x + 5)\\), we distribute each term in the first binomial to each term in the second binomial:\n\n\\[\n(2x + 3)(x + 5) = 2x \\cdot x + 2x \\cdot 5 + 3 \\cdot x + 3 \\cdot 5\n\\]\n\nNow, we perform the multiplications:\n\n1. \\(2x \\cdot x = 2x^2\\)\n2. \\(2x \\cdot 5 = 10x\\)\n3. \\(3 \\cdot x = 3x\\)\n4. \\(3 \\cdot 5 = 15\\)\n\nCombining all these terms, we get:\n\n\\[\n2x^2 + 10x + 3x + 15\n\\]\n\nNext, we combine the like terms \\(10x\\) and \\(3x\\):\n\n\\[\n2x^2 + 13x + 15\n\\]\n\nThus, the expanded form of \\((2x + 3)(x + 5)\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2x^2 + 13x + 15}\n\\]",
